  "content": {
    "id": "p20-q23-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "23",
    "prompt": "For $f(x)=\\dfrac{1-x^2}{x^2+1}$:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p20-q23-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find $f'(x)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f'(x)=-\\dfrac{4x}{(x^2+1)^2}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f'(x)&=\\frac{(-2x)(x^2+1)-(1-x^2)(2x)}{(x^2+1)^2}\\\\f'(x)&=\\frac{-2x^3-2x-2x+2x^3}{(x^2+1)^2}\\\\f'(x)&=-\\frac{4x}{(x^2+1)^2}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q23-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Evaluate $f'(0)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "dependsOn": [
          "p20-q23-a"
        ],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f'(0)=0$",
          "worked": "$$f'(0)=-\\frac{4(0)}{(0^2+1)^2}=0.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q23-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Show that $f(x)$ is even.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f(-x)=\\dfrac{1-(-x)^2}{(-x)^2+1}=\\dfrac{1-x^2}{x^2+1}=f(x)$, so $f$ is even.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(-x)&=\\frac{1-(-x)^2}{(-x)^2+1}\\\\f(-x)&=\\frac{1-x^2}{x^2+1}\\\\f(-x)&=f(x)\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $f(x)$ is even.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 34
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q23-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Hence explain why $f(x)\\leq 1$ for all $x$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "dependsOn": [
          "p20-q23-a",
          "p20-q23-b",
          "p20-q23-c"
        ],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f'(x)>0$ for $x<0$ and $f'(x)<0$ for $x>0$. Thus $f$ has maximum value $f(0)=1$, so $f(x)\\leq1$ for all $x$.",
          "worked": "Since $(x^2+1)^2>0$, $f'(x)<0$ for $x>0$, and $f'(0)=0$. Thus $f$ decreases to the right of $0$. Since $f$ is even, its values to the left of $0$ mirror those to the right; equivalently, $f'(x)>0$ for $x<0$.\n$$f(0)=\\frac{1-0^2}{0^2+1}=1.$$\nTherefore $f$ has maximum value $1$ at $x=0$, so $f(x)\\leq1$ for all $x$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      }
    ]
  },
